        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 73-year-old male patient, admitted on 01/09/2007 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory changes. He was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Clinical monitoring including pulse oximetry and vital signs was maintained throughout. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged home on 02/09/2007 with an optimised inhaler regimen and a short course of oral steroids. I recommend close follow-up and ongoing COPD monitoring in your practice. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
